--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI DrivesListPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable DrivesListDataSource seam whose methods keep
the web hook names at the Swift call sites (loadVehicles ← useSelectedVehicle/GET /vehicles, useDrives
← GET /drives?vehicle_id, useBulkDeleteDrives ← DELETE /drives/bulk). The entire web aggregation layer
(web/src/lib/drivesAggregation.ts) is ported verbatim into the deterministic, unit-tested
DrivesAggregation: getEfficiency (derived Wh/km from the battery delta), the gradeFromEfficiency /
gradeFromNumeric ladders, computePeriodStats, priorPeriod, detectAnomalies / detectNotable /
detectCommutes, groupByDate, and dailyTrend. The structured search (web parseSearchQuery + matchesTokens:
free text + score: / from: / distance:<op> operators) is ported into DrivesSearch.

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the global VehicleSelect + the
date RangePicker) and every region the web source renders:

  the compact summary bar (web PageHeaderSticky → stickySummary), the search field + the live
  "filtering" indicator + the active-filter chips (web SearchInput + ActiveFilterChips), the overview
  KPI card — six metric tiles (Drives / Distance / Drive-time / Avg-score / Efficiency / Cost) each
  carrying its prior-window percent delta, the secondary stats line, and the anomaly callout — or its
  empty panel (web GlassPanel7 + drives.noStatsRange), the "Drives over time" metric-switcher chart
  (drives / distance / score / efficiency / cost; bars for counts/distance/cost, lines for the averaged
  score/efficiency), the collections pill bar (All / Anomalies / Notable / Commutes / Tagged with live
  counts + the disabled Tagged pill), the sort + CSV-export controls, and the date-grouped, bulk-
  deletable (confirm dialog), paginated drive list of DriveCards (grade badge, time + duration +
  distance/no-telemetry/in-progress + high-speed + low-efficiency badges, the route, and the Avg/Max
  speed + battery-delta + efficiency metric chips).

All measurements stay SI canonical in the model (meters / seconds / m·s⁻¹ / Wh); conversion to the
user's unit preference happens ONLY at the SwiftUI render boundary via the shared KMP Units facade +
DriveScoreFormat / DrivesListFormat (ADR-005, SI-cutover instructions). Adaptive across macOS/iPad
regular width vs. iPhone compact (ADR-002/006): the header controls, the six-tile KPI grid, and the
list controls reflow. Every visible literal resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names
(zero hardcoded text; all 65 manifest keys verified present in code). a11y: VoiceOver labels/traits on
the selection control, grade badge, collections bar, sticky summary, chart, and sort controls; Dynamic
Type via the typography tokens; light/dark via the design-token colors. Navigation: registered for the
new .drives route (DrivesRouteRegistration), reachable + deep-linkable via its /drives path segment.
The .drives route is distinct from .driving (which hosts the separate Drive Score surface), mirroring
the web split of /drives (DrivesListPage) vs /drive-score (DriveScorePage).

There is no map (manifest declares 0 maps). The data sources are request/response (drives + bulk
delete), not live SSE streams, so no >2-min staleness indicator applies (ADR-013).

